  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Neighbourhood party music of Dar es Salaam rooted in the drumming of the Zaramo people of the surrounding coast, played at weddings and all-night street dances. Groups combine several hand-beaten drums with a cheap electronic keyboard and a singer, amplified through overdriven loudspeakers, and their rhythms later fed the sampled beats of singeli; the keyboard card stands for the small Casio-type keyboards the groups use.",
